@startuml cls-scheduling
title Class Diagram — Scheduling

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class School <<external — academic>> {
}
class Cohort <<external — academic>> {
}
class Course <<external — academic>> {
}
class AcademicActor <<external — academic>> {
}

enum SessionStatus <<enumeration>> {
  Open
  Closed
  Cancelled
}

class Environment {
  +environmentId: Int
  +schoolId: Int
  +code: String
  +name: String
  +capacity: Int
  +status: Boolean
}

class ScheduleBlock {
  +scheduleBlockId: Long
  +cohortId: Long
  +courseId: Int
  +environmentId: Int
  +instructorActorId: Long
  +dayOfWeek: Int
  +startsAt: Time
  +endsAt: Time
  +create()
}

class ClassSession {
  +classSessionId: Long
  +scheduleBlockId: Long
  +sessionDate: Date
  +openedBy: Long
  +openedAt: DateTime
  +closedBy: Long
  +closedAt: DateTime
  +sessionStatus: SessionStatus
  +open()
  +close(closedBy)
  +cancel()
}

Environment "1" -- "0..*" ScheduleBlock : schedule_block.environment_id FK
ScheduleBlock "1" -- "0..*" ClassSession : class_session.schedule_block_id FK
ClassSession --> SessionStatus

Environment ..> School : environment.school_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
ScheduleBlock ..> Cohort : schedule_block.cohort_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
ScheduleBlock ..> Course : schedule_block.course_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
ScheduleBlock ..> AcademicActor : schedule_block.instructor_actor_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
ClassSession ..> AcademicActor : opened_by / closed_by\n(cross-context, no FK)

note left of ScheduleBlock
  RN-18/RN-20: starts_at < ends_at (chk_block_time).
  The DB unique constraints only catch an identical
  starts_at; real interval overlap (touching ranges
  are fine, e.g. 10:00 end / 10:00 start) is checked
  in application code by ScheduleBlockOverlapGuard
  before every create/update — one query for the
  environment, one for the instructor. Neither
  cohort_id, course_id nor instructor_actor_id is
  ever verified against Academic before saving —
  see 09-microservices/communication-patterns.md §3.
end note

note right of ClassSession
  RN-22: one attendance per actor per session,
  enforced in attendance (uq_attendance_session_actor).
  RN-23 (intended): the session should be Open
  when attendance is recorded -- ms-attendance
  never checks this session's status at all, so
  it is not enforced (corrected 2026-10-12 against
  FULL/). open() can never succeed in practice —
  see ST-01 in diagram-index.md.
end note

note as N1
  All classes also carry the standard audit block
  (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/
  updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) — omitted
  here for readability. See AGENTS.md §2.2 and
  06-data/domains/04-scheduling.md for the
  column-level ER view.
end note

@enduml
